sider the block of 4 Democrats as a single unit. Now we have 6 units to arrange: the block of Democrats and the 5 Republicans.\n\nThe number of ways to arrange these 6 units is given by the factorial of 6, which is \\(6!\\):\n\\[\n6! = 720\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Within the block of 4 Democrats, the 4 Democrats can be arranged among themselves in \\(4!\\) ways:\n\\[\n4! = 24\n\\]\n\nStep 3: To find the total number of ways to arrange the 9 committee members such that all 4 Democrats are together, we multiply the number of ways to arrange the 6 units by the number of ways to arrange the 4 Democrats within their block:\n\\[\n6! \\times 4! = 720 \\times 24 = 17280\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of ways the committee members can sit in a row of 9 chairs such that all 4 Democrats sit together is \\(\\boxed{17280}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{17280}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"counting_and_probability:24"}
